///! net: network primitives + HTTP.
///!
///! Standing up a TCP server or HTTP endpoint should not need
///! external dependencies. This module provides sockets and addresses
///! at the base, with an HTTP layer on top.
///!
///! Datagram and connection sockets, name resolution, an HTTP/1.1
///! layer, TLS, and WebSocket ship in the box. `net::udp` adds
///! connectionless datagrams alongside `net::tcp`; `net::dns` resolves
///! hostnames via `getaddrinfo`; `net::tls` wraps a stream in OpenSSL
///! (with `net::https` on top); `net::ws` speaks RFC 6455 over any
///! `Read + Write` transport (ws:// over TCP, wss:// over TLS).
///!
///! Deliberately out of scope:
///!
///! - **Unix sockets.** Easy to add; no caller has needed them.
///! - **HTTP/2, chunked transfer-encoding, pipelining.** The server is
///!   HTTP/1.1 with keep-alive (persistent connections, read timeouts,
///!   `Connection: close` opt-out); each request is still served
///!   sequentially within a connection.
///! - **Full URL parsing.** `http::Client` takes a `SocketAddr` and
///!   a path; users that need `https://host:port/path` wrap that
///!   in their own parser.
///! - **Unix-domain / raw sockets.** No caller has needed them yet.

namespace std::net;

public module net::ip;
public module net::socket_addr;
public module net::sockaddr;
public module net::tcp;
public module net::udp;
public module net::dns;
public module net::tls;
public module net::ws;
public module net::http;
public module net::https;
